# Security rules (RadarLeb)

Read `docs/security.md` for the full picture, including the credential-rotation
note. This file is a quick checklist for the AI: when you're modifying any of
the files in the globs above, double-check these patterns.

## ⚠️ Top-level concern: rotated credentials

Production RDS credentials were committed to the public repo before today.
They must be rotated. If you're touching anything DB-config-related, verify
`docs/security.md` was acted on first.

## Mass assignment

Every Eloquent model that takes user input must declare `$fillable` (or
`$guarded`).

```php
// ❌ Don't
class User extends Authenticatable
{
    protected $guarded = [];   // wide-open: any column can be set from forms
}

// ✅ Do
class User extends Authenticatable
{
    protected $fillable = [
        'name', 'phone', 'password', 'date_of_birth', 'game_id',
    ];
    // wallet_balance, is_admin, etc. are NOT in $fillable on purpose —
    // they're admin-only fields.
}
```

When accepting input, use a Form Request:

```php
// ❌ Don't
public function update(Request $request, User $user)
{
    $user->update($request->all());   // accepts any field
}

// ✅ Do
public function update(UserUpdateRequest $request, User $user)
{
    $user->update($request->validated());   // only validated fields
}
```

## DevAutoAuth has three layers — keep all three

`app/Http/Middleware/DevAutoAuth.php`:

1. `if (! app()->environment('local')) return $next($request);`  ← env check
2. Hostname check refusing `.com`, `.net`, AWS domains, etc.       ← host check
3. NOT registered in `bootstrap/app.php`.                         ← registration check

Never remove any of them. Never register the middleware in production. Never
change the env check from `local` to a permissive list.

## Two auth guards

Public users go through `web` guard, admins through `admin`. They are
separate. Don't:

```php
// ❌ Don't unify the guards
auth()->user()    // ambiguous — which guard?

// ✅ Do
auth('web')->user()
auth('admin')->user()
```

`PortBasedSessionIsolation` middleware (which is actually path-based — see
`docs/history.md`) keeps the two session cookies from clashing. Don't disable
it on `/admin/*` routes.

## Password handling

```php
// ✅ Storing
'password' => Hash::make($plain),

// ✅ Verifying
if (Hash::check($plain, $user->password)) { /* ok */ }

// ❌ NEVER
'password' => bcrypt($plain),                      // works but Hash:: is preferred
'password' => $plain,                               // ☠️
'password' => md5($plain),                          // ☠️
if ($user->password === $plain) { ... }             // ☠️
```

`User::$hidden` includes `password` and `remember_token`. Don't remove them
from the array — that's what keeps passwords out of JSON responses.

## CSRF & state-changing routes

Every route that mutates state (POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE) must be in the
`web` middleware group, which adds CSRF. The default routes file does this
automatically.

For Inertia, the CSRF token is passed automatically. **Don't disable CSRF**
on a route to "make it work". 419 errors mean a real CSRF mismatch — debug
the cause, don't bypass.

For genuine API endpoints (stateless, no session), use `routes/api.php` and
add Sanctum or signed URLs. We don't have any of those yet.

## Wallet rules — enforced by `WalletTransaction::boot()`

Don't bypass these. If you need a one-off insert, use the model:

```php
// ✅ Through the model — boot hooks run
WalletTransaction::create([
    'user_id'  => $user->id,
    'amount'   => $scan->cost,
    'scan_id'  => $scan->id,
    'game_id'  => $scan->game_id,
    'type'     => 'debit',
]);

// ❌ Direct DB insert — bypasses validation
DB::insert('INSERT INTO wallet_transactions ...');
```

Invariants the model enforces:
- `type` is lowercased on save.
- If `scan_id` is set, `amount` must equal `scans.cost` (1¢ tolerance).
- Top-ups have `game_id = NULL` and `scan_id = NULL`.
- One transaction per scan (UNIQUE partial index on `scan_id`).

## XSS

- Inertia/Vue auto-escapes `{{ value }}` — no special action needed.
- Filament/Livewire auto-escapes its output.
- Blade templates: use `{{ $value }}` (escaped). **Never `{!! $value !!}`**
  unless you've sanitized with `Purifier` first and you have a clear reason.

## SQL injection

- Eloquent and the Query Builder parameterize automatically. Safe by default.
- `DB::statement(...)` and `DB::raw(...)` are NOT parameterized. Use bindings:

```php
// ❌ Vulnerable
DB::statement("UPDATE games SET price_to_play = $newPrice WHERE id = $id");

// ✅ Safe
DB::statement('UPDATE games SET price_to_play = ? WHERE id = ?', [$newPrice, $id]);

// ✅ Even better — use the query builder
DB::table('games')->where('id', $id)->update(['price_to_play' => $newPrice]);
```

We have a few `DB::statement(...)` calls in migrations for portable
correlated subqueries. Those use no user input — they're safe. Don't
introduce user input into raw SQL.

## Secrets in code

- Never commit `.env`. The `.gitignore` enforces this.
- `env('VAR_NAME')` should only be called inside `config/*.php` files. Code
  elsewhere should read `config('section.key')`. This makes config caching
  work (`php artisan config:cache`) — `env()` returns `null` from cached
  config in production.

```php
// ❌ Don't
// In a controller:
$secret = env('STRIPE_SECRET');

// ✅ Do
// In config/services.php:
'stripe' => [
    'secret' => env('STRIPE_SECRET'),
],

// In a controller:
$secret = config('services.stripe.secret');
```

When you add an env var, update `.env.example` so the next dev/AI sees the
field.

## Rate limiting

The `web` group has no rate limiting by default. Add `throttle:N,M` for any
endpoint that's expensive or abusable:

```php
Route::middleware(['auth', 'throttle:30,1'])->group(function () {
    Route::post('/scan/{game}', [GameController::class, 'scan']);
    Route::get('/winners', [WinnerController::class, 'index']);
});
```

`30,1` = 30 requests per minute per user.

## File uploads

We have no user-facing upload endpoints yet. If you add one:

```php
// In a Form Request
public function rules(): array
{
    return [
        'avatar' => ['required', 'image', 'mimes:jpg,jpeg,png', 'max:2048'],
    ];
}

// In the controller — store with a generated name, never the user's name
$path = $request->file('avatar')->store('avatars', 'public');
```

Never trust `$request->file('x')->getClientOriginalName()` for the path.

## Logging

- Don't log passwords, tokens, or wallet amounts in plaintext.
- Use `Log::info('user_action', ['user_id' => $u->id, 'action' => 'scan'])` —
  structured context, not interpolated strings.
- Errors → `Log::error()`. Routine info → `Log::info()`. Debug → `Log::debug()`
  (gated on `APP_DEBUG`).
